+/**
+ * Event: onSelectionGeometryChanged
+ * @event Plugin#onSelectionGeometryChanged
+ * @memberof Plugin
+ * @alias onSelectionGeometryChanged
+ * @description The function called when the ON-SCREEN geometry of the text selection
+ * changes -- either because the selection itself changed, or because it MOVED on
+ * screen (document scroll, zoom). Word editor only.
+ *
+ * Lets a plugin anchor UI to the selection without polling: reading the geometry
+ * through callCommand would truncate the editor's redo stack, so a plugin that polled
+ * on every scroll frame would destroy the user's redo history.
+ *
+ * The handler receives {rect, hasText}, where rect is
+ * {left, top, width, height, corners} in editor-window client pixels (see
+ * asc_GetSelectionScreenRect), or null when there is no text selection -- in which
+ * case hasText is false and anchored UI should hide.
+ */
